lines.extend(['','Material caveat added by this audit','NLRC3 short-window reference reads are not an all-reference haplotype over the wider locus. A separate nearby missense allele is observed on those reads. This does not invalidate the insertion, whose alternate local sequence remains coherent, but longer haplotypes should be reconstructed before making allele-specific protein or peptide claims. The public rs773155391 record has a worst-consequence label of stop_gained, but the observed G>A substitution projects to c.1340C>T / p.Ser447Leu in ENST00000359128.10 (TCG to TTG). Do not apply record-wide labels to a specific allele.','', 'The six events have credible local DNA evidence; RNA support varies from scant to moderate and includes repeated fragment endpoints. They are candidates for matched-normal and orthogonal confirmation, not validated tumor-specific targets. There is no evidence here to change cancer lineage or a treatment regimen. For future peptide work, normal-sample genotyping and patient-specific haplotype reconstruction take priority over generating more predictions from an unclassified alternate allele.','', 'Scope and reproducibility','Scripts and audit-data.json preserve read counts, variant representations, transcript matches, public source matches, and bounded read evidence. Only the six requested loci were fetched from existing indexed BAMs. No full BAM rescan, patient-data upload, or clinical assay occurred. Wider exact-flank filters are a stress test; in RNA they can reduce assessability because of splice junctions and fragment boundaries, not necessarily biological absence. Endpoint signatures are a descriptive check, not a validated duplicate-removal method.','', 'Primary/official references','GENCODE GTF coordinate, exon, CDS and transcript documentation: https://www.gencodegenes.org/pages/data_format.html','Tan et al., Unified representation of genetic variants (2015): https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25701572/','MacArthur et al., A systematic survey of loss-of-function variants in human protein-coding genes (2012): https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22344438/','VCF 4.1 specification, FILTER semantics: https://samtools.github.io/hts-specs/VCFv4.1.pdf'])
